# BOHEMIA SIDE QUEST — PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# S01 — THE METER READER
# Shape: economy-as-morality (electricity). Faction wires: TRADES, NETWORK.
# Systems used AS the mechanic (W9): the ELECTRICITY economy is the whole puzzle;
# the resolution actually shifts NETWORK posture. Grounded in the house-of-cards
# power canon (the grid has no owner; the network skims covertly) and the
# Amalgamation blind-spot canon (the skim runs DOWN toward the water — the deep
# tunnel / reclaim plant where the secret sleeps; looking under it is the danger,
# not player strength). No proper names anywhere (W8). CLOUT rides HOW you resolve
# it, never a label (Paolo 7/21): quiet fix -> #quiet, public patch -> #notable,
# loud spectacle -> #reckless. The player does not pick a clout number; the
# loudness of the DEED sets it.

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# The corpus this quest is actually built from. Every id below resolves in
# records/BOHEMIA_QUESTBOOK_LAW_INDEX.json (3,672 citable findings mined out of
# the 152 studied quests in questbook/), and gates/quest_study_gate.js verifies
# the id AND the quoted law title verbatim. A citation is a claim the machine
# can check, never a name-drop.
# @STUDY Q003.W1  THE DIRTY ERRAND
#   applied: the ask is compromised before you leave: the lineman needs it quiet because he has a family and you are cheaper to lose, and he says so.
# @STUDY Q092.W2  THE INSTITUTION IS THE MONSTER
#   applied: the thing drinking the current is not a man, it is an arrangement nobody can name, and looking for the name is what costs.
# @STUDY Q002.W2  THE BRANCH-ROUTER NPC
#   applied: the fixer at the tap is the single node the whole quest forks through: quiet fix, public patch, or spectacle.
# @STUDY Q003.P1  W1 (dirty errand
#   applied: the ports master asks for exactly this: seed the moral weight in the HIRE, so the lineman admits up front that you are the cheaper person to lose.
#
# ---- AND THE VOICE PASS (WORDS lane, 8/26/26). Same structure, same stages,
# ---- same branches, same effects. Only the WORDS changed. The card is
# ---- laws/BOHEMIA_VOICE_CARD_8_26_26.md and the counts that forced it are in
# ---- records/BOHEMIA_VOICE_DIAGNOSIS_8_26_26.md: this scene was the flattest
# ---- one in the build (sentence spread 3.36 against a corpus median of 6.82)
# ---- and it contracted twice in 39 lines.
# @STUDY Q142.W6  SILENCE EXTRACTS
#   applied: the lineman volunteers his kid and his fear when the player says nothing back, and the silent option reaches the same node as the spoken one, so refusing to talk is never punished with less.
# @STUDY Q152.W5  THE DESPAIR SCENE CHANGES REGISTER, ONCE
#   applied: he is practical the whole way through and drops it exactly twice, four words each time -- "I've got a kid" and "Please" -- and never explains either one.
# @STUDY Q100.N2  NODE LYNETTE_MINEFIELD
#   applied: the fixer launders his own job in front of you ("I don't steal it, I move it") and the run-on he does it in is the characterization; the polite word for the ugly thing, dared you to say the ugly one.
# @STUDY Q004.N1  NODE SPIRIT_OFFER
#   applied: the trap answer refuses to sell certainty at any depth -- he does not know whose current it is, he says so plainly, and no option anywhere in the quest can buy the name.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_meter_reader   The Meter Reader
@ACT     1
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

# ---- ROLES. Cast at runtime against whoever exists. Never a hardcoded name.
@ROLE lineman  REQ  faction=TRADES  block=browned
@ROLE fixer    OPT  faction=NETWORK met_before=false

@STAGE 10
  @LOG Nine at night, every night, half this block goes brown.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20
  @LOG Line tests clean. Clean and browning out means somebody's on our feed. Found the split.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG Put the current back myself. Block has light tonight. Nobody knows it was me.
  @DO bond lineman +15
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Handed the tap to the trades. Daylight patch, every name on the work order.
  @DO faction TRADES +8
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 COMPLETE #reckless
  @LOG Cut the skim line in front of the whole block. Sparks, a crowd, and somebody upstream has my face now.
  @DO faction_posture NETWORK +1
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 33 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Left it alone. Block goes dark again tonight, same hour.

@OBJ 10  "Find why the block browns out"   target=lineman
@OBJ 20  "Follow the skimmed line"         target=fixer

# =====================================================================
# THE ASK. The theme is in the FIRST line, not a missable node (W3).
# =====================================================================
@TALK open  speaker=lineman  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY Nine at night. Every night, nine, and half this block goes brown. #tired
  @SAY I tested it myself. Line's clean. Clean and browning out means somebody upstream is on my feed drinking before we do.
  @SAY So walk it back for me. Past the dead storefronts, follow whatever cable's running warm. You any good at quiet?
  @OPT "I'll walk it."                 [gate: none]  -> walk  @DO learn line_is_clean
  @OPT "Why not you?"                  [gate: none]  -> why
  @OPT "Not my block."                 [gate: none]  -> refuse
  @OPT (say nothing, just go)          [gate: none]  SILENCE -> walk  @DO learn line_is_clean
  @NOVERB "Tell me who runs the network"
@END

@TALK why  speaker=lineman
  @SAY Because everybody on this block knows my face. I've got a kid. #dread
  @SAY Whoever's drinking that current doesn't like being looked at. You're new. Nobody comes asking if you don't come back.
  @OPT "Comforting."                   [gate: none]  -> walk  @DO learn line_is_clean
  @OPT "Who doesn't like being looked at?"  [gate: none]  -> why2
@END

@TALK why2  speaker=lineman
  @SAY If I knew, I wouldn't need you. I asked my foreman about it once. He just looked at his hands till I stopped talking.
  @SAY Follow the split. Don't make a show of it. Please.
  @DO set_stage 20
@END

@TALK refuse  speaker=lineman
  @SAY Yeah. Fair. I'll go ask somebody else's kid to do it. #tired
  @OPT "Maybe another night."          [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 33
  @OPT "Fine. I'll look."              [gate: none]  -> walk  @DO learn line_is_clean
@END

@TALK walk  speaker=lineman
  @SAY Good. Splits somewhere past the dead storefronts. Warm cable. You'll feel it before you see it. #tired
  @DO set_stage 20
@END

# =====================================================================
# THE SPLIT. You catch the skimmer. They are not a monster (W7) — they are
# faster than the meter. The fork is loudness, and loudness is the cost.
# =====================================================================
@TALK split  speaker=fixer  entry=stage>=20
  @SAY Easy. Easy, easy. Don't touch that, it's live. #wary
  @SAY I don't steal it. I move it. The grid doesn't belong to anybody so there's nothing there to steal, I'm just faster than the meter. That's it.
  @SAY So. Put it back and go home and nobody hears a thing about it, or make it loud. Which are you?
  @OPT "Put it back. Nobody hears it."  [gate: none]  SILENCE -> put     @DO set_flag saw_the_skim
  @OPT "The trades should see this."     [gate: none]  -> report          @DO set_flag saw_the_skim
  @OPT "Whose current is it?"            [gate: none]  TRAP -> whose      @DO set_flag saw_the_skim
  @OPT (cut the tap, right now)          [gate: none]  -> cut             @DO set_flag saw_the_skim
  @NOVERB "Turn them in for a bounty"
@END

# THE TRAP OPTION (W-craft): asking the wrong question near the secret costs.
# It goes DOWN, toward the water — the reclaim plant, per canon. Looking is the
# danger, not fighting. This sets the unrecorded flag the fold reads later.
@TALK whose  speaker=fixer
  @SAY Huh. That's the one question, isn't it. I don't know whose. Never have. #dread
  @SAY It runs down. Not up. Down, toward the water. That's where I quit asking and you should quit there too.
  @SAY I told you nothing. Understand me. Put it back or don't, it's your block and it's your face they'll remember.
  @OPT "Put it back. Quietly."          [gate: none]  SILENCE -> put  @DO learn it_goes_down
  @OPT "Cut it. Let them see."           [gate: none]  -> cut          @DO learn it_goes_down  @DO set_flag looked_under_the_rock
@END

@TALK put  speaker=lineman
  @SAY Light's back. I'm not going to ask how. #tired
  @SAY You didn't make a show of it. I noticed. Not going to say anything else about it.
  @OPT "Just fixed a line."             [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 30
  @NOVERB "It was the network"
@END

@TALK report  speaker=lineman
  @SAY You brought it to us. Could've kept it to yourself and you didn't. #tired
  @SAY We patch it in daylight. Names on the work order, mine first, then the crew, then yours if you want it up there.
  @OPT "Do it in daylight."             [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 31
@END

@TALK cut  speaker=lineman
  @SAY You cut it in front of everybody. Somebody's kid was clapping. Nobody's mother was. #dread
  @SAY They felt that upstream. Somebody up there has your face now. I don't know what else to tell you.
  @OPT "Let them know my face."          [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 32
  @OPT (say nothing)                     [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 32
@END
